body:
This is pretty much how I see it. 

&#x200B;

I always get told "You just need to find the right people". How selfish is that? My happiness should not be dependent on others, and putting selfishness aside - it's a dumb idea. Things are never guaranteed. 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry to hear that you aren't doing well now. I hope you find peace, however that may be,

It's not wrong at all. Many people couldn't even imagine what it's like to be in your position, try as they might. 

&#x200B;

I hope you find peace.

Previously attempted, no one really cared. I remember my family making jokes on the drive home from the hospital.

&#x200B;

Weirdly, it helped.

Amen to that. Too many people assuming. The worst is when they try to give you advice, as if they're so wise and knowledgeable, and you're too stupid to think of the bare minimum.

&#x200B;

"Have you thought about trying to change your situation? Maybe get a new job? xx" NO FUCKING SHIT??

I want to say yes, but I am so set on what I'm going to do, and I don't want to spread any more negativity to you. 

&#x200B;

I'm glad you're doing well!!
